# Copy to `.env` (in mobile/) and fill in. Restart Metro with `npx expo start -c`
# after any change. Everything here is EXPO_PUBLIC_* — it ships in the app bundle,
# so ONLY put public/rate-limited values here (never a private key or secret).

# ---- Works with defaults (leave blank to use free public endpoints) ----
# Solana RPC — the public defaults are rate-limited, which makes sends (especially XGO /
# Token-2022 transfers that also create the recipient's token account) time out, and treasury
# deposit history fail to load. Point this at your backend's RPC proxy so one operator-provided RPC
# is shared by all users and the key stays server-side:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc
# (or a direct Helius URL — but that embeds the key in the app bundle).
EXPO_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC=
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEVNET_RPC=
# EVM RPCs — public defaults work; set your own (Alchemy/Infura/QuickNode) for real use.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ETH_RPC=
EXPO_PUBLIC_BSC_RPC=
# Prefer routing every network through the backend /api/rpc proxy (keys stay server-side, one
# shared RPC for all users, and it relaxes the client's rate throttle so loads are fast):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_DEVNET_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=solana-devnet
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_ETH_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=ethereum
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_BSC_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=bsc
# Treasury-pool preference threshold for XGO swaps (bps). Default 150 (1.5%).
EXPO_PUBLIC_TREASURY_MAX_WORSE_BPS=

# ---- Needed to fully test specific features ----
# EVM transaction history (Home + Activity). Free key at etherscan.io/apis (one key,
# all EVM chains). Without it, EVM history is simply hidden.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ETHERSCAN_KEY=
# dApp connect (WalletConnect). Free project id at cloud.reown.com.
#
# THIS IS WHAT LETS YOU SCAN A DESKTOP SCREEN AND SIGN ON YOUR PHONE. Without it the scanner
# (Wallet tab, QR icon) opens to a notice instead of a camera, and the whole transport is inert —
# no relay connection is even attempted.
#
# The Goshen web app must use the SAME project id. A mismatch pairs and then silently fails to
# relay, which looks like the wallet ignoring the site.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
# Push-notification backend (Phase 2, see /notify-service). When set, the app registers this
# device's addresses so you get "Received" pushes even when the app is closed. In-app receive
# alerts (while open) work without it. Requires an EAS dev build + an EAS projectId in app.json.
EXPO_PUBLIC_NOTIFY_API=

# ---- Treasury / launch config (leave blank while testing) ----
# The main Global Goshens communal treasury address, shown on the Ecosystem tab. Blank = the
# built-in address in src/config/treasury.ts, which is the real treasury — so you only set this
# to point a build somewhere else. This is independent of any multisig: connecting a Squad never
# changes what the treasury view displays.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOSHENS_TREASURY=
# Squads v4 multisig treasury address (optional pre-set). Usually left blank — you create or
# connect a Squad in-app (More → Multisig treasury), which stores it on the device. If set,
# it's the default multisig until you connect a different one. The multisig is its own feature
# and does NOT change the Global Goshens treasury view above.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MULTISIG=
# Community swap fee (0.44% on non-XGO swaps). SOLANA: the treasury WALLET that owns the fee
# token accounts; the fee is taken in the output token and deposited into that wallet's token
# account for the mint (created on-chain automatically on first use).
#
# Leave BLANK unless you specifically want fees going somewhere other than the treasury above —
# it now follows that address rather than repeating it, so the Ecosystem screen can't advertise
# one account while the money lands in another. Setting this makes them differ, deliberately.
# EVM: the treasury's 0x address for EVM swaps (blank disables EVM fees entirely).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_FEE_OWNER=
EXPO_PUBLIC_EVM_FEE_RECIPIENT=
# 0x liquidity in the swap comparison (adds 0x alongside keyless KyberSwap).
# Prefer the proxy (key stays server-side). Embedded key is a fallback.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ZEROX_PROXY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_ZEROX_API_KEY=

# ─── Association platform (sign-in and the Vault) ────────────────────────────
# The server that verifies who is calling and serves what they own. Both surfaces
# live on the same host, so one variable covers them: the platform mounts /v1
# under its API prefix, and the app builds `${API}/v1/auth/challenge` from this.
#
# Include the API prefix. For the Goshen platform that is /_api, NOT /api —
# Replit's edge intercepts the literal /api/ prefix and 502s it:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_API=https://your-host/_api
#
# Blank is a working no-op: no sign-in happens, the Vault opens public links, and
# everything falls back to the chain and the on-device cache. Setting it switches
# the platform path on with no app release.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_API=
# The domain the platform is allowed to name in a challenge. The wallet refuses to
# sign any message that doesn't contain it, so this must match the server's
# AUTH_DOMAIN *exactly* — a mismatch fails on the phone, before the server ever
# hears about it, and looks to a member like sign-in silently not working.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_DOMAIN=
# Only needed if sign-in and the Vault ever move to different hosts; each falls
# back to the two above.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_API=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_DOMAIN=
#
# ─── The Goshen web app (the SITE, not the API) ──────────────────────────────
# The other half of the system. The wallet holds keys and proves what you own;
# the web app is where you buy, browse communities, and issue — and whatever you
# get there lands back here as a Key. More → Marketplace and → Issue a Key open
# it in the bridged browser.
#
# This is the site root with no API prefix, e.g. https://goshen.example — NOT the
# /_api value above, even when the two share a host. https only: the app refuses
# anything else rather than handing it to a browser that has the wallet bridged
# into it.
#
# Blank leaves both rows visibly disabled, which is the honest default until the
# web app is deployed somewhere a member can reach.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEBAPP_URL=
#
# NOTE ON NETWORKS: the challenge names the cluster and the server refuses one it
# doesn't speak for. This app defaults to mainnet-beta; the platform server
# defaults to devnet. A deployment that leaves the server's SOLANA_CLUSTER unset
# therefore refuses every real sign-in with a cluster mismatch. Set it there.
